        The below examples will show rolling mean calculations with window sizes of
        two and three, respectively.

        >>> s = pd.Series([1, 2, 3, 4])
        >>> s.rolling(2).mean()
        0    NaN
        1    1.5
        2    2.5
        3    3.5
        dtype: float64

        >>> s.rolling(3).mean()
        0    NaN
        1    NaN
        2    2.0
        3    3.0
        dtype: float64
        r»␀␀c␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ó(␀␀␀•—␀t␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀‰|␀␀␀|||¬«␀␀␀␀␀␀S␀rS␀␀)r]␀␀r»␀␀rT␀␀s␀␀␀    €re␀␀␀r»␀␀zRolling.mean¨␀␀s%␀␀␀ø€␀ôV␀‰w‰|Ø%ØØ'ğ␀ó␀
